<title>UK: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>		     19/12/96		 12/12/96	    22/12/95</p>
<p>    GASOLINE	    400			400		   475</p>
<p>    NAPHTHA	  75-100			 75		    50</p>
<p>    GAS OIL   2,050-2,100	    2,000-2,000		 1,650</p>
<p>    FUEL OIL	    350			350	     325-350</p>
<p>    JET KERO	     25			 25		    10</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks were unchanged with fresh deliveries few and offtake to inland markets slack.</p>
<p>Naphtha  inventories were slightly higher with deliveries outpacing  petrochemical and blending demand.</p>
<p>ARA Gas oil tanks were swelled a little by deliveries from Russia with importers well stocked after this weeks weather-led price rises amid muted end-user buying intererst.</p>
<p>Russian supplies topped up fuel oil stocks after good bunkering offtake and some covering by power utilities .</p>
<p>Jet stocks were steady with only light blending offtake.</p>
<p>-- Colin Wooster, London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7456</p>
</text>
